Subject: [PATCH] Do not warn about identical target-specific dependency names

cargo-udeps 0.1.61 visits dependencies from multiple target tables. Reusing
one package under the same dependency name is valid, including when each
target enables different features. Only a different name for the same
package makes the package-to-name mapping ambiguous.

Keep the existing warning for distinct names and leave unused-dependency
analysis unchanged.

--- a/src/lib.rs
+++ b/src/lib.rs
@@ -830,5 +830,7 @@
 					let names = &mut this[dep.kind()];
 					names.by_extern_crate_name.insert(extern_crate_name, dep.name_in_toml());
 					if let Some(pkg) = names.by_package_id.insert(to_pkg.package_id(), dep.name_in_toml()) {
-						shell.warn(format!("duplicate package mentioned in toml {}. {pkg}", to_pkg.package_id()))?;
+						if pkg != dep.name_in_toml() {
+							shell.warn(format!("duplicate package mentioned in toml {}. {pkg}", to_pkg.package_id()))?;
+						}
 					}
